{"id":"sf-bodies-outside-city-payroll","tier":"OFFICIAL","title":"The San Francisco payrolls the City’s own pay file leaves out","question":"What do the school district, City College, BART, the Golden Gate Bridge district, the Superior Court and the transport authorities pay, and how much is overtime and other pay?","finding":"8 public bodies in San Francisco report to the State but are not in the City’s payroll file. In the latest year on file: San Francisco Unified School District 2021: 10,664 paid positions, $623.9 million in wages, overtime 0.3% and other pay 27.1% of regular pay; City College of San Francisco (Community College District) 2022: 1,836 paid positions, $120.8 million in wages, overtime 12.2% and other pay 1.6% of regular pay; BART 2025: 4,573 paid positions, $619.5 million in wages, overtime 17.6% and other pay 10.5% of regular pay; Golden Gate Bridge, Highway and Transportation District 2025: 898 paid positions, $88.5 million in wages, overtime 8.0% and other pay 2.7% of regular pay; San Francisco Superior Court 2025: 547 paid positions, $60.3 million in wages, overtime 0.1% and other pay 6.6% of regular pay. Years missing from the export as saved: San Francisco Unified School District 2020, 2022, 2023, 2024, 2025; City College of San Francisco (Community College District) 2023, 2024, 2025; Golden Gate Bridge, Highway and Transportation District 2020. The 2025 file for school districts was not among the files saved. The San Francisco Housing Authority does not appear in any of the files.","how":"State Controller raw export, every row reported by each body, 2019 to 2025 as saved. Wages are the export’s total wages; benefits are left out. The export does not say whether a year is a calendar or a fiscal year. San Francisco’s overtime here is $480.3 million for 2024; the City’s own payroll file has $468.9 million for fiscal 2024 and $471.0 million for fiscal 2025, so the two sources are close but not the same and are not mixed in any one figure.","lim